From ca09728478f9709cad44309ca6e76cebba743f6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhizhenS <ZhizhenS@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:57:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix the panel pointer: stuck on some openings, left on
 screen after closing

Two faults in the PanelOverPicture input feed, both read from the R294 log on
Stellar Blade (DcompOverlay=1, Scaler=0, raw input).

Left on screen: feed_input sets MouseDrawCursor on the GPU 1 runtime, which
ReShade does not feed, so nothing clears it when the panel closes. Because
reshade_overlay keeps that runtime's ImGui frames running, the pointer stayed
drawn. The log showed cursor=1 with a frozen position after close, and that
position matches the stray pointer in a screenshot.

Stuck: the mouse hook won as soon as it had seen one event. Of eight openings,
five saw no hook event and fed from the game runtime, moving normally; three
got a few hook events and the written position stayed fixed for the whole
opening while the game runtime's pointer kept moving. Reopening until no hook
event arrived is why it seemed to fix itself. Whichever pointer moved last is
now the one used. A title whose game runtime freezes under the input block
never moves that pointer, so it keeps the hook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
