From 14687c8c3d47b1f9b7ef3935afe8adf779835813 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhizhenS <ZhizhenS@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:57:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix horizontal bands with frame generation (BB1)

present_frame cleared every frame's back buffer before copying the picture over
it, on a chain of 2 buffers. With the game focused the chain runs in Independent
Flip with immediate flips, and the clear colour reached the screen as flickering
dark horizontal bands. Screenshots missed them because capture reads after the
copy. Dyeing the clear magenta turned the bands magenta; removing it removed them.

- Clear only when the picture will not cover the chain (a crop smaller than the
  back buffer). A failed enlarge falls back to a crop, so it brings the clear back.
- PresentBuffers (2-6, default 6, panel slider, restart) sets the chain's buffer
  count. The open panel, drawn after the copy, flickered in game-image bands until
  the count went up, so the clear was one visible stage of a wider problem.
- PresentRaceProbe=1 keeps the magenta clear as a diagnostic needing no special build.
- The scaler's descriptor sets are per buffer instead of two, and its pointer slot
  moves past them; the old fixed slot 20 would have collided with buffer index 2.

Probe results on two RTX 5080s, 4K 120 Hz, Stellar Blade, driver 621.01:
2 buffers bands at 2X; 3 and 4 clean or nearly clean at 2X, a few bands at 4X;
6 clean at both. Focused present-to-display p50: 0.50 ms with 2, 0.39 ms with 6,
both with PresentLatency1=1.

Not established: why the screen reads a buffer still being written. The buffers
needed rise with the frame generation multiplier, which fits flips queued ahead
of the screen, but that is inference. Why the focused chain reports SyncInterval
0 under Present(1, 0) is also open. The scaler path was reviewed, not run, and
present-to-display with PresentLatency1=0 and 6 buffers was not measured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
